{"status": "ok", "message-type": "work-list", "message-version": "1.0.0", "message": {"facets": {}, "total-results": 1985524, "items": [{"institution": [{"name": "Koninklijke Brill NV", "acronym": ["BRILL"]}], "indexed": {"date-parts": [[2026, 3, 3]], "date-time": "2026-03-03T08:45:01Z", "timestamp": 1772527501280, "version": "3.50.1"}, "reference-count": 0, "publisher": "Walter de Gruyter GmbH", "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "DOI": "10.1163/2210-7975_hrd-9824-2014064", "type": "dataset", "created": {"date-parts": [[2016, 2, 18]], "date-time": "2016-02-18T22:15:31Z", "timestamp": 1455833731000}, "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 1, "title": ["A Long Way to Go"], "prefix": "10.1163", "member": "374", "container-title": ["Human Rights Documents online"], "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2026, 3, 3]], "date-time": "2026-03-03T07:49:40Z", "timestamp": 1772524180000}, "score": 27.004572, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://www.degruyterbrill.com/database/hrdo/entry/hrdo.HRD-9824_2014-064/html"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[null]]}, "references-count": 0, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.1163/2210-7975_hrd-9824-2014064"}, {"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2026, 7, 13]], "date-time": "2026-07-13T11:49:28Z", "timestamp": 1783943368301, "version": "3.55.0"}, "description": "Article A003: The Shape of Global Health: The world has come a long way, but still has a long way to go", "reference-count": 0, "publisher": "International Monetary Fund (IMF)", "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "DOI": "10.5089/9781484315422.022.a003", "type": "component", "created": {"date-parts": [[2026, 7, 13]], "date-time": "2026-07-13T00:47:57Z", "timestamp": 1783903677000}, "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 1, "title": ["The Shape of Global Health: The world has come a long way, but still has a long way to go"], "prefix": "10.5089", "author": [{"given": "David", "family": "Bloom", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}], "member": "3029", "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2026, 7, 13]], "date-time": "2026-07-13T00:47:58Z", "timestamp": 1783903678000}, "score": 26.195398, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://elibrary.imf.org/view/journals/022/0051/004/article-A003-en.xml?cid=41379-com-dsp-crossref"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[null]]}, "references-count": 0, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.5089/9781484315422.022.a003", "relation": {"is-component-of": [{"id-type": "doi", "id": "10.5089/9781484315422.022", "asserted-by": "object"}]}}, {"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2026, 8, 12]], "date-time": "2026-08-12T15:52:24Z", "timestamp": 1786549944538, "version": "build-2736575974"}, "posted": {"date-parts": [[2016]]}, "group-title": "SSRN", "reference-count": 27, "publisher": "Elsevier BV", "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "abstract": "<jats:p>The paper throws light on micro credit in India and under given circumstances it would survive or not. It started as small groups formed to help themselves or the self help groups. One of the benefits is that it is very accessible. Banks don\u2019t provide loans to those with little to no assets, and generally don\u2019t give small size loans. The borrowing increased year after year and low income groups were supported as much as possible. There are many challenges within microfinance initiatives which may be social, financial, administrative and political. Here, some community members may cheat poorer or less-educated borrowers. But increasing default cases alarmed Microfinance Institutions to get hold of flaws in the system. Microfinance Institutions (Development and Regulation) Bill 2012 was introduced with a view to monitor the sector. The Bill was needed to strengthen the regulatory framework and consumer protection norms of the microfinance industry in India. An ordinance was made after a series of suicide incidents as a result of abusive practices of MFIs such as charging high interest rates, adopting coercive collection practices and lending aggressively beyond the repayment capacity of the borrowers rather than helping the poor get out of poverty. Policy makers must make strategies to help MFIs and borrowers as well. Repayment is less because of the loopholes in the lending procedures. Hopefully Standing Committee on Finance pays sufficient attention to these critical issues.</jats:p>", "DOI": "10.2139/ssrn.2742761", "type": "posted-content", "created": {"date-parts": [[2016, 3, 9]], "date-time": "2016-03-09T11:02:28Z", "timestamp": 1457521348000}, "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 0, "title": ["Microfinance - Long Way to Go"], "prefix": "10.2139", "author": [{"given": "Dr Anil Kumar", "family": "Kothari", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Liza", "family": "Jain", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}], "member": "78", "reference": [{"key": "ref1", "journal-title": "Annapurna Microfinance Pvt Ltd"}, {"key": "ref2", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "journal-title": "Arohan Financial Services Pvt Ltd", "DOI": "10.17501/wcosm.2017.2110"}, {"key": "ref3", "journal-title": "Asirvad Microfinance Pvt Ltd"}, {"key": "ref4", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "journal-title": "Bandhan Financial Services Pvt Ltd", "DOI": "10.17501/wcosm.2017.2110"}, {"key": "ref5", "author": "Pvt Bss Microfinance"}, {"key": "ref6", "author": "Credit Cashpor Micro"}, {"key": "ref7", "journal-title": "Disha Microfin Pvt Ltd"}, {"key": "ref8", "journal-title": "Equitas Microfinance Pvt Ltd"}, {"key": "ref9", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "journal-title": "ESAF Microfinance and Investments Pvt Ltd 10. Fusion Microfinance Pvt Ltd", "DOI": "10.17501/wcosm.2017.2110"}, {"key": "ref10", "journal-title": "Grama Vidiyal Micro Finance Ltd"}, {"key": "ref11", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "journal-title": "Grameen Financial Services Pvt Ltd", "DOI": "10.17501/wcosm.2017.2110"}, {"key": "ref12", "journal-title": "Janalakshmi Financial Services Pvt Ltd 14. Madura Micro Finance Ltd"}, {"key": "ref13", "article-title": "Adhikar Microfinance Pvt Ltd 2", "journal-title": "ASA International India Pvt Ltd 3. Belstar Investment & Finance Pvt Ltd"}, {"key": "ref14", "journal-title": "Chaitanya India Fin Credit Pvt Ltd 5. Future Financial Services Ltd 6. Growing Opportunity Finance (India) Pvt Ltd"}, {"key": "ref15", "article-title": "Indian Cooperative Network for Women Ltd 10. M Power Micro Finance Pvt Ltd 11. Mahasemam Trust 12. Margdarshak Financial Services Ltd 13. Pahal Financial Services Pvt Ltd 14. Rashtriya Seva Samithi 15. Sahara Utsarga Welfare Society 16. Sahayog Microfinance Ltd 17. Saija Finance Pvt Ltd 18. Samhita Community Development Services 19. Sanghamitra Rural Financial Services 20. Sarala Women Welfare Society 21. Shikhar Microfinance Pvt Ltd 22. Uttrayan Financial Services Pvt Ltd 23. Vedika Credit Capital Ltd 24", "journal-title": "Humana People to People India 8. IDF Financial Services Pvt Ltd 9"}, {"key": "ref16", "journal-title": "To provide legitimacy and a proper regulatory framework to MFIs and others involved in delivery of financial services to low-income people (Legitimacy for Microfinance Institutions and Players)"}, {"key": "ref17", "journal-title": "To ensure that MFIs indeed satisfy the broader objectives for which they have come into being (in the first place) and also that they operate and function in a sound and legal manner, in accordance with norms and standards required of such (pro-poor financial) institutions. This would also involve ensuring that MFIs (and especially the NBFC MFIs) don't operate like moneylenders"}, {"key": "ref18", "journal-title": "To protect clients from MFI bad practices like coercive repayment, abusive interest rates, fraudulent products and the like (Protection of Microfinance Clients)"}, {"key": "ref19", "journal-title": "To protect MFIs that operates legally and correctly from usury laws (Protection of MicroFinance Institutions)"}, {"key": "ref20", "journal-title": "To prevent micro-finance crisis situations like what happened in AP (Andhra Pradesh) in 2010 (Prevention of Micro-Finance Crisis Situations)"}, {"key": "ref21", "article-title": "Microfinance firms can play role in financial inclusion: RBI", "author": "Murali Ramkrishna", "year": "2015", "journal-title": "The Economic Times"}, {"key": "ref22", "author": "N Srinivasan", "year": "2010", "journal-title": "Microfinance India: State of the Sector Report"}, {"key": "ref23", "author": "Sharma Manoranjan", "year": "2007", "journal-title": "India's Transforming Financial Sector"}, {"key": "ref24", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.4135/9788132108115.n3", "author": "Nair Tara", "year": "2013", "journal-title": "Tankha Ajay Microfinance India: State of the Sector Report"}, {"key": "ref25", "year": "2010", "journal-title": "Regulatory Issues in Microfinance Sector: A Case Study of Andhra Pradesh"}, {"key": "ref26", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1349/ddlp.830", "volume": "17", "year": "2014", "journal-title": "The Hindu"}, {"key": "ref27", "author": "Girija Srinivasan", "year": "2013"}], "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2026, 8, 12]], "date-time": "2026-08-12T15:08:31Z", "timestamp": 1786547311000}, "score": 25.275253, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://www.ssrn.com/abstract=2742761"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[2016]]}, "references-count": 27, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.2139/ssrn.2742761", "published": {"date-parts": [[2016]]}, "subtype": "preprint"}, {"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2025, 8, 26]], "date-time": "2025-08-26T06:40:24Z", "timestamp": 1756190424517, "version": "3.44.0"}, "posted": {"date-parts": [[2017, 10, 3]]}, "group-title": "Article", "reference-count": 0, "publisher": "The Conversation", "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "DOI": "10.64628/ab.ve4gcvy